# ── Client data — never publish ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The workbook names real officials, real allegations and named citizens, and
# the derived link list reveals which posts an office is monitoring. Both are
# the client's working intelligence, not project source. `npm run test:sheet`
# reads sheet-links.json and says so plainly when it is absent.
Eluru_Social_Listening.xlsx
*.xlsx
scripts/sheet-links.json


# Throwaway probe scripts written by research agents — never commit these.
scripts/_*.ts

# Sample dataset for local demos. Built from real published news by the real
# classifier, so it carries "suspected fake" judgements about named outlets and
# real people — that must not live in a public git history.
public/sample-data.json

# Build scaffolding and archived notes — working material, not project source.
# The redesign specs were written to brief agents during a UI rebuild, and
# docs/history holds superseded status files from an earlier session.
docs/

# Real session cookies for real accounts. Never commit.
.scraper-profile/

# Live social sessions — same sensitivity as the profile itself.
.scraper-session.json
.desk-pull/

# Named citizens' comment text, read through a signed-in browser. Megabytes of
# it, rewritten whole on every walk, in a public repository. public/sample-data.json
# is ignored for the same reason: this is other people's words, and a scraper
# intermediate has no business in the history.
scraper/demo-comments.json
